---
import Breadcrumb from "../components/Breadcrumb.astro";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { site } from "../config/site";
import { webPageJsonLd } from "../lib/seo";

const title = "Terms of Use | Landscaping Calculators";
const description =
  "Terms for these landscaping calculators. Results are ordering estimates, not a construction specification, and densities vary by load.";
const pathname = "/terms/";
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} jsonLd={webPageJsonLd({ title, description, pathname, breadcrumb: "Terms" })}>
  <header class="page-intro">
    <Breadcrumb current="Terms" />
    <h1>Terms</h1>
    <p class="lede">The terms for using {site.legalName}. Last updated {site.updatedLabel}.</p>
  </header>
  <article class="prose">
    <h2>Estimates, not a specification</h2>
    <p>
      The calculators estimate how much gravel, mulch, topsoil, or sod to order from measurements
      you supply. They are an arithmetic aid. They are not an engineering design, a drainage plan,
      a soils report, or a substitute for the supplier’s scale ticket.
    </p>
    <p>
      Bulk density changes with moisture, gradation, and compaction. The presets are published on
      the <a href="/methodology/">methodology page</a> with their sources and their limits. A load
      can weigh more or less than the preset. Bag and pallet sizes vary by brand and farm. You are
      responsible for the measurements you enter and for confirming the order with the seller.
    </p>
    <p>
      Depth comments on the calculator pages are general US practice for ordering. A driveway, a
      retaining base, a trench, or a lawn renovation can require a different section than the
      example loaded in the form. Where the page says to calculate layers separately or to ask the
      farm about a partial pallet, that instruction is part of using the result.
    </p>

    <h2>No warranty</h2>
    <p>
      The site is provided as is. There is no warranty of accuracy, fitness for a particular
      project, or uninterrupted availability. To the extent the law allows, the publisher is not
      liable for a short load, a heavy load, a wrong measurement, or a cost estimate that left out
      delivery and tax. The price fields are material-only arithmetic on the quantity shown.
    </p>

    <h2>Units</h2>
    <p>
      Unless a label says otherwise, tons are US short tons of 2,000 pounds, yards are cubic yards
      of 27 cubic feet, and currency amounts are US dollars. Metric results are conversions of
      those quantities. The international foot used in the conversion is 0.3048 meters.
    </p>

    <h2>Use of the site</h2>
    <p>
      You may link to the calculators. You may not present the pages as a product of someone else,
      and you may not copy them into another site in a way that implies a partnership that does
      not exist. The material presets are not endorsements.
    </p>
    <p>
      Do not misuse the site, attempt to break the hosting, or send automated traffic that
      interferes with other readers. The pages are static. There is nothing to log into.
    </p>

    <h2>Advertising</h2>
    <p>
      This version shows labeled empty boxes where an ad could go later. Those boxes are not
      advertisements and do not load a third-party script. If ads are added, the
      <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a> will say so before the scripts are turned on.
    </p>

    <h2>Law and contact</h2>
    <p>
      {site.publisherName} publishes this site as a personal project, not as a company. There is
      no street address and no phone number. Questions about the terms can go to the email on the
      <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>. The <a href="/disclaimer/">disclaimer</a> covers the
      limit of the estimates. These terms do not name a state venue.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
